.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
explores every interleaving of a set of protocol nodes, the network
between them, their timeouts and their crashes, up to the budgets given,
and checks the properties in every state it reaches.
.Pp
With
.Fl -model-file ,
the nodes are the program you ship, run unmodified as processes; the
model file names the program, the environment to explore and the
invariants.
That is the way to check a product; see
.Sx Checking a program
below,
.Lk https://gregburd.codeberg.page/libcmc/reference/model-file/ "the model file" ,
and
.Xr cmc 7 .
.Pp
With
.Fl -model ,
the nodes are an in-process model: C step functions written against
.Xr libcmc 3 .
That interface is the engine's calibration path: the
.Cm hc
core reproduces TLC's results on a published consensus specification.
The rest of this page, from
.Sx Choosing the model and properties ,
describes it.
.Pp
.Nm make install
installs
.Nm .
A program that embeds the engine with in-process models of its own
writes a
.Fn main
that passes its table of models to
.Fn cmc_main ,
and links against
.Pa libcmc.a ;
that program is a
.Nm
too.
The binary built by this repository carries the in-process models
.Cm hc
(the calibration core),
.Cm toy ,
and
.Cm toy-bug1
to
.Cm toy-bug3 .
.Pp
Output follows the wording of TLC, the TLA+ model checker, so the two can
be compared line by line.
Depth counts the initial state as 1.
.Ss Checking a program
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -model-file Ar file
Check the program the model file names, with its environment and
invariants.
Linux x86-64 only: the nodes run under seccomp user notification.
Every key the file sets must be one
.Nm
implements; an unknown or unsupported key is an error, not ignored.
.It Fl -binary Ar path
Check this program instead of the file's
.Cm binary ,
for example a build with a planted bug.
It must be a non-PIE executable
.Pq built with Fl no-pie .
.It Fl -spec Ar file
Model-check an abstract specification
.Pq a Pa .cml No module
on its own, the way TLC checks a TLA+ module: no implementation, just
the declared variables, actions and invariants.
As in TLC,
.Cm and
and
.Cm or
evaluate left to right and short-circuit, so a guard can protect a
division or a function application.
Variables are integers in a set, functions on integer keys
.Pq Li [K -> T] ,
records
.Pq Li [a : T, b : T]
and sequences of at most N elements
.Pq Li Seq(T, N) ;
a value outside its variable's type, a sequence past its bound
included, is a model error (exit 3), never cut.
A type's sets are constant expressions; one that reads a variable is
refused.
An arithmetic result of 2^40 or more in magnitude is an overflow
(exit 3).
.Li def NAME(p, ...) = EXPR
declares a named operator, expanded where it is used; a def may use
only the defs before it, so recursion is refused.
A reachable state in which no action is enabled is a deadlock: it is
reported with the shortest trace, in TLC's words
.Pq Dq Error: Deadlock reached. ,
and exit status 1, unless the model says
.Cm deadlock = off
or
.Fl -no-deadlock
is given.
A
.Cm constraint
and an
.Cm action_constraint
bound the search as TLC's
.Cm CONSTRAINT
and
.Cm ACTION_CONSTRAINT
do.
A
.Cm property
is
.Cm eventually Ar E ,
.Ar A Cm ~> Ar B ,
or the action property
.Cm always [ Ns Ar E Ns Cm ]_vars ,
TLA+'s
.Li [][E]_vars :
every step that changes a variable satisfies
.Ar E ,
an expression over
.Ar x
and
.Ar x' .
.Cm fairness weak
and
.Cm fairness strong
make every action weakly or strongly fair
.Pq Li WF_vars , SF_vars ;
.Cm fair weak Ar action
and
.Cm fair strong Ar action
make one action so.
The fairness of a parameterized action is that of its disjunction over
the parameters, as
.Li WF_vars(A)
is for the
.Li \eE
the emitted module gives it.
See
.Lk https://gregburd.codeberg.page/libcmc/reference/plan-tlaplus-scope/ "the TLA+-scope plan" .
.Pp
A
.Ar file
named
.Pa *.tla ,
or given with
.Fl -config ,
is a TLA+ module, checked with its TLC configuration: the
.Fl -config
file, or by default the
.Pa .cfg
beside the module, as TLC finds it.
The module is translated to the
.Pa .cml
model it means and that model is checked, so the verdict, counts and
trace are the ones the
.Pa .cml
gives.
The reader takes one module that
.Cm EXTENDS
only Naturals, Integers, FiniteSets, Sequences and TLC;
.Cm CONSTANTS
bound in the configuration to integers,
.Cm TRUE ,
.Cm FALSE ,
model values or sets of those;
.Cm VARIABLES ;
definitions
.Li Op(p, ...) == e ,
each seeing only those above it, expanded where they are used;
.Cm ASSUME
of
.Li C \e in Nat ,
.Li Int
or
.Li BOOLEAN ;
an
.Li Init
that is a conjunction of
.Li x = e ;
a
.Li Next
that is a disjunction of actions, each a conjunction of guards,
.Li x' = e ,
.Li x' \e in S
and
.Cm UNCHANGED ,
under
.Li \e E
parameters; and
.Li Spec == Init /\e [][Next]_vars
with
.Li WF_vars(A)
and
.Li SF_vars(A)
conjuncts, each A one action of Next.
A
.Cm THEOREM
and its proof are skipped.
An
.Cm INVARIANT
whose conjuncts are all
.Li x \e in T
.Pq a TypeOK
gives the variables their types, which the checker enforces on every
state.
One invariant does so: TypeOK if the configuration lists it, else the
first of that form; every other invariant is checked as written, as is
one whose T reads a variable.
Expressions are the
.Pa .cml
set: integers, booleans,
.Li \e in ,
.Li \e A ,
.Li \e E ,
.Li Cardinality ,
functions, records, sequences and tuples,
.Cm EXCEPT
with paths and
.Li @ ,
.Cm IF ,
and bullet lists of
.Li /\e
and
.Li \e/
laid out as TLA+ defines them.
A variable's type is inferred from
.Li Init
and the actions; an integer is any of TLC's, a sequence holds at most
12 elements.
The configuration may give
.Cm CONSTANT(S) ,
.Cm SPECIFICATION
or
.Cm INIT
and
.Cm NEXT ,
.Cm INVARIANT(S) ,
.Cm PROPERTY Ns / Ns Cm PROPERTIES
.Pq Li <>P , Li "P ~> Q" No and Li [][A]_vars ,
.Cm CONSTRAINT(S) ,
.Cm ACTION_CONSTRAINT(S) ,
.Cm CHECK_DEADLOCK ,
.Cm SYMMETRY
of
.Li Permutations(C)
for a set C of model values, and a
.Cm VIEW
of all the variables.
Anything else, such as
.Cm LET ,
.Cm CHOOSE ,
strings, set operators, a constant substitution
.Pq Li <- ,
or a fairness condition
.Pa .cml
does not have, is refused with its line and name (exit 3).
So is what SANY or TLC would stop on: a
.Li /\e
beside a
.Li \e/
without parentheses, a parameter or bound name that names something
already declared, and arithmetic or order on a model value.
.Fl -define
is refused: a module's switches are its constants.
.It Fl -config Ar file
The TLC configuration for a TLA+ module read with
.Fl -spec
or
.Fl -emit-cml .
.It Fl -emit-cml Ar file.tla
Print the
.Pa .cml
model a TLA+ module and its configuration translate to, as
.Fl -spec
would check it.
.It Fl -coverage
With
.Fl -spec ,
after the search print, per action, what TLC's
.Fl coverage
prints for it,
.Ar distinct : Ns Ar generated
.Pq the new states it found, and every successor it produced, a stutter or a state already seen included ,
and the number of explored states that enable it.
An action that no explored state enables is named in a warning: it is
vacuous in the model.
The distinct counts match TLC's.
The generated counts can differ where a guard has an existential or a
disjunction: TLC produces a successor per witness and per true
disjunct, cmc one per successor.
.It Fl -no-deadlock
With
.Fl -spec ,
do not report a deadlock, as TLC's
.Cm CHECK_DEADLOCK FALSE ;
with
.Fl -emit-tla
and
.Fl -emit-cfg ,
write the module and configuration for a model whose deadlock check is
off.
.It Fl -trace-out Ar file
On a violation, also write the counterexample cmc prints to
.Ar file ,
in the format
.Fl -trace-format
names.
.It Fl -trace-format Cm itf | json
The format of the
.Fl -trace-out
file; without
.Fl -trace-out
it is an error.
With
.Fl -spec ,
.Cm itf
(the default) is the Informal Trace Format that Apalache writes and its
tools read
.Pq Lk https://apalache-mc.org/docs/adr/015adr-trace.html ,
laid out as Apalache lays out a counterexample for the module
.Fl -emit-tla
writes: an integer is
.Ql {\(dq#bigint\(dq: \(dqN\(dq} ,
a function is
.Ql {\(dq#map\(dq: [[k, v], ...]} ,
a record is an object of its fields in the order of their names, a
sequence is an array, and each state's
.Ql #meta
names the action that led to it.
.Cm json
is an array of states, each with its
.Ql index ,
its
.Ql action
.Pq null for the first
and its
.Ql vars .
With
.Fl -model-file ,
only
.Cm json
(the default) is offered: one object per listed step, with the
.Ql action
as printed, its
.Ql number
.Pq null for an unnumbered step ,
and the world after it, each node's
.Ql state
and
.Ql durable
records and whether it is
.Ql crashed ,
and the
.Ql replies .
With
.Fl -refine ,
each object also has a
.Ql spec :
the world in the terms of the abstract spec, null where the
refinement check does not judge it (between two nodes' steps, or inside
one), else
.Ql state ,
the bound abstract variables' values, and
.Ql action ,
the abstract action the step refined, with its parameters, or
.Ql stutter
.Pq Fl -refine-steps ; null without it .
With
.Fl -spec ,
a liveness violation writes its lasso: in
.Cm itf
the states of the prefix and the cycle, with ADR-015's
.Ql loop
holding the index of the state the cycle goes back to and the header's
.Ql #meta
naming that last action as
.Ql loopAction
.Pq Ql Stuttering No when the cycle stutters ;
in
.Cm json
the same states, then the loop state again with that action and a
.Ql back_to
index.
No file is written on a pass.
A file that cannot be written is exit 3.
.It Fl -emit-tla Ar file
Translate the abstract specification
.Pq a Pa .cml No module
to TLA+ on standard output, so it can be checked with TLC or Apalache
and proved with TLAPS.
Records, sequences and defs become their TLA+ forms, and each variable
carries an Apalache
.Li @type
annotation.
Name the output after the module
.Pq Pa NAME.tla
so TLC accepts it.
The module defines
.Li TypeOK ,
each variable in its declared type, and, when an invariant is marked
.Li [inductive] ,
.Li IndInv
.Pq TypeOK and the marked invariants ,
the constants' values as an
.Li ASSUME ,
and the theorem
.Li Spec => []IndInv
with a TLAPS proof outline: Init => IndInv, IndInv /\e [Next]_vars =>
IndInv', and the temporal step by
.Li PTL ,
followed by Spec => []NAME for each marked invariant.
TLAPS may need more steps where an obligation leans on facts it lacks
.Pq Cardinality , for one .
A model that declares one of the names TypeOK, IndInv, ConstOK, PTL or
Inductive is refused.
.It Fl -check-inductive
With
.Fl -spec ,
check that the invariants marked
.Li [inductive] ,
with TypeOK, form an inductive invariant: they hold in the initial
state, and every step of every action from
.Em every
state of the declared types that satisfies them, reachable or not,
leads to a state that satisfies them.
This is the check Apalache makes with
.Li --init=IndInv --inv=IndInv --length=1 .
Every value of every variable's type is enumerated; a product of more
than 1,000,000 states, or a function of more than 12 keys, is exit 3.
A counterexample to induction (a state and the step out of the
invariant, with the action's parameters) is exit 1.
A model with no marked invariant, or with a constraint, is exit 3.
.It Fl -emit-cfg Ar file
Write the TLC configuration for the module
.Fl -emit-tla
writes: its constants, TypeOK and every invariant, property, state and
action constraint by name, and
.Cm CHECK_DEADLOCK FALSE
when the deadlock check is off.
.It Fl -define Ar tag
Activate an action gated with
.Op Ar tag
in a
.Pa .cml
spec; repeatable.
Used to turn on a planted-bug action.
A tag that gates no action in the spec is an error.
.It Fl -refine Ar spec
Check that the implementation named by
.Fl -binary
or the model file
.Em refines
the abstract
.Ar spec
.Pq a Pa .cml No module .
At each reached implementation state the abstract invariants are
checked against the mapped state, so one abstract model validates many
implementations.
A counterexample is shown in spec terms too: below each listed step
after which the check judges the world, a
.Ql spec:
line gives the abstract state the binding built there (the bound
variables only) and, with
.Fl -refine-steps ,
the abstract action the step refined
.Pq Ql init , Ql stutter , or Ql NAME(p=v, ...) .
Requires
.Fl -bind .
.It Fl -bind Ar file
The binding
.Pq a Pa .bind No file
that maps the implementation's observables onto the abstract variables,
for
.Fl -refine .
Each spec variable is bound at most once, a function variable entry by
entry; a line the reader cannot use is an error.
A binding builds integers and functions of integers only: a record or
sequence variable, or a function of them, is refused.
.It Fl -refine-steps
Check refinement at the level of
.Em steps ,
not only states (Milestone C2): each implementation transition must map
to an abstract action step or a stutter (the abstraction unchanged).
This catches a step the abstract model forbids even when every state it
reaches satisfies the invariant, which
.Fl -refine
alone cannot.
Requires
.Fl -refine ,
and every spec variable must have a
.Pq Bq map
entry
.Pq it refuses otherwise ,
since matching an abstract action step needs the whole abstract state.
.It Fl -crashes Ar n , Fl -drops Ar n , Fl -timeouts Ar n
Override the file's budgets.
.It Fl -depth Ar d
Bound the search to
.Ar d
actions, at least 1; a search that reaches it is reported as incomplete.
With
.Fl -simulate ,
the length of each walk, default 100.
.El
.Pp
.Fl -bfs ,
.Fl -simulate ,
.Fl -seed ,
.Fl -walks ,
.Fl -max-states
and
.Fl -time
work as for in-process models, except that walk
.Va i
of a simulation does not take its own seed: the same
.Fl -seed
takes the same walks.
A world in which a node has run more than one thread is never merged
with another
.Pq see Xr cmc 7 ,
so a threaded program's search is a tree; without
.Fl -max-states
it stops, incomplete, after 1000000 such worlds.
Any other option with
.Fl -model-file
is an error.
.Ss Choosing the model and properties
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -model Ar name
The model to check, by its name in the program's model table.
Required, except with
.Fl -replay .
.It Fl -cfg Ar key Ns = Ns Ar value Ns Op , Ns ...
Core settings, passed to the core's
.Fn cfg_set .
May be given more than once; later settings override earlier ones,
including those read by
.Fl -tlc-cfg .
.It Fl -tlc-cfg Ar file
Read a TLC
.Pa .cfg
file: its
.Sy CONSTANTS
become core settings, and its
.Sy INVARIANTS
and
.Sy PROPERTIES
become the properties to check.
A keyword may stand on its own line or share one with its items, as in
.Ql INVARIANT TypeOK .
Any other keyword
.Pq Sy SYMMETRY , Sy CONSTRAINT , Sy VIEW and the rest
or line cmc cannot read is an error.
.It Fl -inv Ar name Ns Op , Ns ... , Fl -prop Ar name Ns Op , Ns ...
Check these properties.
The two options are synonyms; each property's kind comes from the model.
.It Fl -all-props
Check every property of the model.
.It Fl -list
Print the model's property names and exit.
.It Fl -version
Print the libcmc version and exit.
.El
.Pp
A model may mark its first properties as always checked.
At least one property must be named, or
.Fl -all-props
given.
.Ss Choosing the search
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -bfs
Breadth-first search, the default.
It finds a shortest counterexample, and its state counts are exact.
.It Fl -dfs Ar depth
Depth-first search to
.Ar depth
states.
A search that reaches the bound without finishing is reported as
incomplete, never as a pass.
.It Fl -simulate
Seeded random walks, not exhaustive.
Walk
.Va i
uses seed
.Ar n Ns + Ns Va i ;
a violation is reported with the
.Fl -seed
and
.Fl -walks Cm 1
that reproduce it.
.It Fl -seed Ar n
First seed for
.Fl -simulate .
Default 0.
.It Fl -walks Ar k
Number of walks for
.Fl -simulate ,
at least 1.
Default 1000.
.It Fl -depth Ar d
Length of each walk, in states.
Default 100.
.It Fl -replay Ar file
Run a replay file written by
.Fl -trace-out
through the real cores, printing each state.
The model, settings and budgets are taken from the file; an option on
the command line that conflicts with the file is refused.
.It Fl -det
Determinism gate: run every step twice from copies of the same state and
fail if the two runs differ in their outputs or their next state.
.It Fl -max-states Ar n
Stop after
.Ar n
distinct states.
.It Fl -time Ar seconds
Stop after
.Ar seconds
of wall time.
.El
.Pp
Every number an option takes must be a whole decimal number in its
range; anything else, such as
.Ql --crashes x ,
is an error rather than a 0.
.Ss Choosing the environment
These options apply to message-passing cores (actor mode).
Each budget is a count over the whole run, from 0 to 255.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -clients Ar n
Client requests each node may receive.
Default 1.
.It Fl -drops Ar n
Messages the network may lose.
In the FIFO network a drop resets one connection: every queued message
on it is discarded and each end's next call fails with
.Er ECONNRESET ,
the way a TCP reset or a partition appears, never a byte lost from the
middle of a live stream.
With
.Fl -model-file
this is the only drop semantics; the actor engine's
.Fl -net Cm bag
may instead lose a single message.
Default 0.
.It Fl -dups Ar n
Messages the network may duplicate.
Needs
.Fl -net Cm bag ,
so it applies only to the actor engine, not
.Fl -model-file .
Default 0.
.It Fl -crashes Ar n
Crashes, of any node.
A crash keeps any prefix of the node's pending disk writes and loses the
rest and the volatile state; a peer reading a connection to the crashed
node gets EOF once that channel drains.
The actor engine then restarts the node; with
.Fl -model-file
a crash is final unless the model's
.Ic restarts
budget lets a
.Sy RESTART
action relaunch the node as a fresh process that reads its surviving
durable record back on startup
.Pq see Xr cmc 7 .
With no restart budget a crash does not come back.
Default 0.
.It Fl -net-cap Ar n
Messages in flight at once.
Default 8.
.It Fl -persist-cap Ar n
Pending disk writes per node.
Default 2.
.It Fl -reply-cap Ar n
Client replies recorded in the ghost log.
Default 8.
.It Fl -timer-cap Ar n
Timers armed at once on one node, each named by its id and argument.
Default 16.
.It Fl -wake-cap Ar n
Wakes pending at once on one node, each named by its id and argument.
Default 8.
.It Fl -drift Ar r
For
.Fl -model ,
how far, per thousand, a node's clock may run slow or fast against
another's, 0 to 500.
When a timed timer fires, one other node's clock may move at the slowest
or the fastest rate this allows; rates in between, and two clocks off
the common rate at once, are not explored.
Default 0.
.It Fl -max-time Ar t
For
.Fl -model ,
the horizon, in the core's time unit: a state whose reference time
passed
.Ar t
is not expanded, and a run that reached one ends INCOMPLETE, never with
a pass.
Messages, client requests, flushes and wakes take no time; only a timed
timer moves the clocks.
A model that arms timed timers needs this, unless it stops arming them
itself or the run is to end at
.Fl -max-states .
.It Fl -req-cap Ar n
Slots in the request log of a model that keeps one
.Pq see Xr libcmc 3 :
one per node that takes clients times
.Fl -clients .
A log that does not fit is an error before the search starts.
Default 8, at most 64.
.It Fl -net Cm fifo | bag
.Cm fifo ,
the default, has one ordered channel per pair of nodes, as TCP does, and
never duplicates.
.Cm bag
is an unordered multiset that may duplicate.
.It Fl -live-steps Ar k
Bound, in steps of the fair schedule, for eventually-properties.
Each round of the fair schedule drains the pending messages before it
fires the armed timers, but nodes that keep messaging each other in a
cycle cannot postpone a timer.
The verdict is about this one schedule, not every fair one.
Default 1000.
.El
.Pp
Going past a cap is reported as an engine error, never silently
truncated.
.Ss Output
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -trace-out Ar file
On a violation, write the counterexample as a replay file.
For
.Fl -spec
and
.Fl -model-file ,
see
.Sx Checking a program .
.It Fl -progress Ar seconds
Print a progress line every
.Ar seconds
during breadth-first search; 0 turns it off.
Default 60.
.It Fl -quiet
Do not print the counterexample.
.It Fl -coverage
Print, for each action kind, the states it generated and the new
distinct states it found.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev CMC_PRELOAD
The path of
.Pa cmc-preload.so ,
the library every checked node runs under.
By default it is found beside the running program (a build tree), then
in
.Pa ../lib/libcmc
from it (an installed
.Pa bin/cmc ) .
A program of your own that calls
.Fn cmc_main
must set it.
A node it did not load into is an error.
.It Ev CMC_ARENA_MB
The size, in MiB, of the preload's deterministic arena.
Default 64; raise it for a target that allocates more.
A value out of range falls back to the default.
.It Ev CMC_STATE_FD , Ev CMC_DURABLE_FD
Set by the checker for each node to the volatile
.Pq 3
and durable
.Pq 193
state-hook descriptors.
A program that keeps its state hook in the build it ships guards every
emit on
.Ev CMC_STATE_FD
so it writes nothing outside a check.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa *.model
Model files; see
.Lk https://gregburd.codeberg.page/libcmc/reference/model-file/ "the model file" .
.It Pa cmc-preload.so
A deterministic heap and a logical clock for the checked program.
.It Pa *.replay
Replay files.
A header names the model, settings and budgets; each following
.Ql act
line is one action in hexadecimal, with its description as a comment.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
No property was violated, and the search was complete for its mode:
breadth-first or depth-first search finished, the walks ran, or the
replay ended.
.It 1
A property was violated, an engine rule was broken (determinism,
durability, a cap), or a witness was never reached.
.It 2
Incomplete: a state, time or depth limit stopped the search before it
finished, with no violation found.
.It 3
Usage error, a bad setting, a model file that cannot be used, or a
replay file that cannot be run.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Check a server as it ships, then a build of it with a planted bug:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ cmc --model-file kvserver.model
\&...
Model checking completed. No error has been found.
$ cmc --model-file kvserver.model --binary ./kvserver-bug
Error: Invariant no_lost_ack is violated.
\&...
.Ed
.Pp
Check a TLA+ module with its TLC configuration, as TLC would, and print
the
.Pa .cml
it reads as:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ cmc --spec logrep.tla --config logrep_read_safe.cfg
\&...
21213 states generated, 4439 distinct states found, 0 states left on queue.
The depth of the complete state graph search is 16.
$ cmc --emit-cml logrep.tla --config logrep_read_safe.cfg
.Ed
.Pp
Check every property of the toy lock server, an in-process model:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ build/cmc --model toy --all-props
\&...
Model checking completed. No error has been found.
\&...
49 states generated, 34 distinct states found, 0 states left on queue.
The depth of the complete state graph search is 11.
.Ed
.Pp
Find the planted bug in
.Cm toy-bug1 ,
save the counterexample, and replay it:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ build/cmc --model toy-bug1 --inv Mutex --trace-out bug1.replay
Error: Invariant Mutex is violated.
  2 clients in the critical section
\&...
$ build/cmc --replay bug1.replay --inv Mutex
.Ed
.Pp
Check a calibration configuration against its TLC result:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ build/cmc --model hc \e
    --tlc-cfg calib/hc/cfg/hc_paper_cp_n3_s1.cfg --det
.Ed
.Pp
Search a large space by random walks first:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ ./mycmc --model mymodel --all-props --crashes 1 --drops 1 \e
    --simulate --seed 7 --walks 100000 --depth 60
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libcmc 3 ,
.Xr cmc 7
.Pp
The guide and design notes:
.Lk https://gregburd.codeberg.page/libcmc/
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Greg Burd Aq Mt greg@burd.me
.Sh CAVEATS
A pass covers only the budgets given.
Raise
.Fl -clients ,
.Fl -drops
and
.Fl -crashes
until the bugs you planted are caught, and treat a run stopped by
.Fl -max-states
or
.Fl -time
as "no violation found in N states".
.Pp
.Fl -net Cm bag
allows behaviour a FIFO transport never shows, so a counterexample found
in bag mode may be spurious for a protocol that relies on FIFO order.
